WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.411
Every later slice is proven without a bike, a backend or a database. This slice

00:00:07.411 --> 00:00:09.607
builds what stands in for them.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.654
One shared fixture surrounds the app: a fake Bluetooth stack, answers for the API,

00:00:15.654 --> 00:00:18.229
and a ride hub that speaks SignalR.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:25.760
A spec offers a fake bike. Every write the page makes is recorded as hex, and the

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.332
spec pushes notifications on demand.

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:35.809
Nothing happens unasked. A Bluetooth call the spec did not expect fails it, and the

00:00:35.809 --> 00:00:37.450
failure names the call.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:44.993
Requests to the API get the answers the spec declared.

00:00:45.338 --> 00:00:47.999
A request nobody answered fails the spec.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:57.179
The ride hub plays SignalR's JSON protocol: the handshake, then invocations both

00:00:57.179 --> 00:00:59.495
ways, once the spec opens it.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:07.970
On the backend, a real SignalR client connects to the API hosted in memory. Without

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:10.740
a session, negotiation is refused.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.065
Time moves only when a test moves it: a fake clock in every fixture, and an event

00:01:17.065 --> 00:01:19.380
probe that waits without sleeping.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.616
Riders see nothing new. Every spec now opens Home inside the doubles, from a phone

00:01:27.616 --> 00:01:28.713
to a desktop.

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:37.750
What the tests prove: twelve behaviour specs, three proving the guard fails a spec,

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:40.848
and eighteen backend tests, all on this machine.

00:01:43.237 --> 00:01:47.840
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:48.185 --> 00:01:52.697
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:52.697 --> 00:01:54.368
every hill and interval.

00:01:54.713 --> 00:01:59.891
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:59.891 --> 00:02:05.339
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:02:05.339 --> 00:02:08.329
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:02:08.675 --> 00:02:11.167
A custom workout lives under Profile.
